WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.099
Speaker 1: All right.

00:00:01.099 --> 00:00:06.250
Was the Trump CNN town hall the most corrosive
television event in political history?

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:07.980
Depends who you ask.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:15.379
For example, Republican Congressman Byron
Donalds was actually reinvigorated into continuing

00:00:15.379 --> 00:00:21.310
to not answer the simple question did Trump
win in 2020 or did he lose?

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:25.349
Trump setting the tone during the town hall
that he's insisting he won.

00:00:25.349 --> 00:00:27.529
Byron Donalds asked about it.

00:00:27.529 --> 00:00:33.570
He will not acknowledge nearly three years
later that Trump simply lost that day.

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:36.329
This is one of the reasons why these events
are so corrosive.

00:00:36.329 --> 00:00:37.980
Listen to this oversight committee.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:40.230
Speaker 2: Can I just say are the facts?

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:42.750
You do acknowledge Donald Trump lost the 2020
election, correct?

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:46.160
Speaker 4: Again, we're going to continue
to talk about 2018 at home.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:50.511
You want me tell you let me tell you why most
voters are frankly kind of tired of y'all

00:00:50.511 --> 00:00:51.511
bringing this up.

00:00:51.511 --> 00:00:52.511
Inflation, water.

00:00:52.511 --> 00:00:56.500
You don't have the courage to express your
memory about Republican voters.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:58.309
Speaker 2: I'm a Republican voter.

00:00:58.309 --> 00:01:02.609
Speaker 4: Just want to talk about inflation,
the border Fed and all the debt ceiling foreign

00:01:02.609 --> 00:01:03.609
policy.

00:01:03.609 --> 00:01:06.750
If you want to talk about the 2020 election,
let's talk about this.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:12.530
We do know that Marc Elias was in many jurisdictions
suing to actually change election procedures,

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:17.479
which, by the way, is at the hands of the
state legislature in every state, according

00:01:17.479 --> 00:01:21.730
to the Constitution, not in the hands of courts,
not in the hands of the Supreme Court, the

00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:22.730
state legislature.

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:24.500
We do know that to be a fact.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:25.500
We do know that.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:29.600
True won't state your opinion about actually
factually what happened in the 2020.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:30.870
Guys want me to make a stick.

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:32.220
And Frank, let me tell you right now, this.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:33.960
Speaker 1: This is not a trick question.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.860
They act like it's a trick question.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:37.390
It's just, okay, fine.

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:39.320
You want Trump to have won.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:41.290
You want him to win in 2024.

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:42.550
You think Biden's bad?

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:45.620
But can we just start with Biden did win.

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:46.890
Can we start there?

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:48.159
They refuse.

00:01:48.159 --> 00:01:53.530
Joe Scarborough from MSNBC just this morning
had actually a pretty good take about the

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:55.160
impact of this town hall.

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:57.600
Speaker 4: No surprises.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:02.200
And yet it was just it was a disgraceful performance.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:03.490
Yes.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:10.240
I'm constantly telling people not to catastrophize
over Trump that he's actually going to lose.

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:13.590
Speaker 1: This is a former Republican member
of Congress, by the way.

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:20.010
Speaker 4: Because he keeps drilling down
deeper and deeper into his base.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:23.360
But it is it is.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:28.860
I can't believe I'm I'm going to use catastrophizing
language here.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:33.750
But it was it was just it was disgraceful
on every level.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.050
Yeah, it showed.

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:41.761
I wouldn't say it's dangerous for democracy
because we passed that a long time ago, but

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:48.780
it showed the corrosive effects of Trumpism
over eight years.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:53.459
And I've got to say.

00:02:53.459 --> 00:03:02.730
I The most shocking part was an audience who
cheered on a president who tried to overturn.

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:03.730
American democracy.

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:04.730
Speaker 1: Yeah.

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:06.170
Joe Scarborough is completely right.

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:11.220
Now, a practical question becomes, did Trump
convince anybody one way or the other?

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:14.890
We'll get to Van Jones, his take on what it
did to Democrats.

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:19.739
But they actually had a focus group on CNN
with a group of Trump supporters.

00:03:19.739 --> 00:03:24.819
And you may or may not be interested to hear
that it didn't affect any of them one way

00:03:24.819 --> 00:03:25.849
or the other.

00:03:25.849 --> 00:03:29.870
Trump spending that time just lying and lying
and lying, it just had no impact one way or

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:30.870
the other vote.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:34.190
Speaker 4: But that's what they have in common,
that most of them are Trump supporters.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:38.950
What I want to ask you, first of all, is do
you think a show of hands anybody think Donald

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:41.720
Trump looks better after this town hall?

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:45.379
And if you think he looks worse, know him.

00:03:45.379 --> 00:03:48.310
Do you think the same thing about him as you
did when you walked in there?

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:53.549
Speaker 1: So on Trump supporters, it had
no impact whatsoever.

00:03:53.549 --> 00:03:54.900
What about on Democrats?

00:03:54.900 --> 00:04:00.599
Well, Van Jones says if you watch this and
you're a Democrat, you're probably feeling

00:04:00.599 --> 00:04:02.650
a lot better about Joe Biden all of a sudden.

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:08.700
Speaker 4: I think if you're a Democrat watching
that, you you think we've been criticizing

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:11.530
and complaining about Biden.

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:14.390
This is a horror show that we don't want a
rerun of.

00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:20.269
And I think a lot of Democrats were appalled
by his behavior and throwing Ukraine under

00:04:20.269 --> 00:04:21.430
the bus.

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:26.090
You know, I hope he gets sued again this morning
for for libel and slander and everything else.

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:31.620
He's being so horrible, you know, toward the
people who have been on their side of his

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:32.620
legal cases.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:39.800
But, you know, I think that we've got to be
careful here now, because Trump has a particular

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:41.550
trick that he uses with nostalgia.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:47.580
The whole Make America Great Again is about
the was this era that was wonderful.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:48.580
Was 19.

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:49.580
Yeah.

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:50.580
Speaker 1: Which we've talked about before.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:57.850
So, listen, I think the best case scenario,
as atrocious and disgusting as the event was

00:04:57.850 --> 00:05:04.750
on the merits, the hope is Trump supporters
still support him.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:07.680
Other Republicans were maybe appalled.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:11.889
And of course, Democrats may be appalled enough
that now they are more interested in coming

00:05:11.889 --> 00:05:16.050
out to vote in 2024 against Trump if he is
indeed the nominee.

00:05:16.050 --> 00:06:11.039
It's still a while to go, but let's hope that's

00:06:11.039 --> 00:06:40.159
the outcome.

